gencruxmitersmt.c, README.upstream and generate-some-aigs-and-cnfs.sh were
written by Armin Biere (Johannes Kepler University Linz, now University of
Freiburg).  They are not published in a public repository; Armin Biere sent
them to Laurent Simon and agreed, in September 2026, to their being part of
SAT Heritage.  They carry no licence of their own: ask him before reusing them
elsewhere.

The CRUX miters they produce were used in the SAT Race 2019 and, beyond the
competitions, in work on distributed cube and conquer and on tuning for cubing.
